{"id": "EUVD-2026-96092", "enisaUuid": "e06ec712-2fad-3ee5-a824-e58e8f92cd8b", "description": "The FV Player 8 plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Arbitrary File Upload in all versions up to, and including, 8.1.7 via the check_mimetype function. This is due to insufficient file type validation in check_mimetype(), which writes attacker-supplied remote file content to the public uploads directory before any MIME or extension check, combined with a missing capability check on new player creation. This makes it possible for authenticated attackers, with subscriber-level access and above, to upload files that may be executable, which makes remote code execution possible. This requires successfully exploiting a race condition.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T05:30:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-11T16:55:17", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://www.wordfence.com/threat-intel/vulnerabilities/id/5c75cb7b-1ebe-411c-8664-848d741e40d4?source=cve", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/fv-player/trunk/models/checker.php#L105", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/fv-player/trunk/models/checker.php#L148", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/fv-player/trunk/models/checker.php#L181", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/fv-player/trunk/models/db.php#L46", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/fv-player/trunk/models/db.php#L1102", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/fv-player/trunk/models/db.php#L1173", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/fv-player/trunk/models/db-video.php#L855", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/fv-player/trunk/controller/editor.php#L36", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/browser/fv-player/trunk/controller/frontend.php#L1211", "https://github.com/foliovision/fv-wordpress-flowplayer/releases/tag/8.1.8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p776-3xx4-5fcg", "CVE-2026-83526"], "assigner": "Wordfence", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdPr